  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Video demonstrating the issue: https://youtu.be/JqiQ6Y0ev3I (Youtube, 39 seconds).\n\nAt certain angles, it can happen while looking straight on as well, the light in the world and on avatars will flicker off and on differently in each eye. Mostly happening in mirrors. So far only happening in The Box world. I will add more worlds if I find them.\n\nThis is similar to what was happening in Unity 5.6 with lighting, but it is more extreme now and far more prominent on the world and avatars by flickering in and out differently in each eye at random.\n\nSome of my setup details:\n- GTX 1080ti\n- Windows Mixed Reality\n- Resolution of 2136x2136 per eye\n\nMy initial thoughts are it could be unity version related again. It was broken in 5.6, then fixed in .15f1 now might be broken differently in .28f1. Although it could also just be mirror related or hopefully only world lighting related. Im reporting it as is right now because it just looks to be similar to the unity 5.6 issue.",
